{"evidence":["Targeted validation passed: `cargo test -p tank_core --test shrimp_chloride_protection`, `cargo test -p tank_core test_chloride_protection_ratio`, and `cargo test -p tank_core --test events threshold_event_summaries_use_explicit_chemistry_units` all succeeded.","`compute_effective_nitrite_hazard` is wired into the existing hourly nitrite accumulator at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:83-90` and the daily condition nitrite factor at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:359-364`.","`chloride_protection_factor` is a named runtime/species parameter with defaults and preset data wiring at `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:300-309`, `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs`, and `crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml`."],"findings_or_gaps":["Medium: `crates/tank_core/tests/shrimp_chloride_protection.rs:89-99` does not model the requested salt-treatment emergency. It starts a second simulation with chloride already elevated from hour 0, instead of raising chloride during an ongoing high-nitrite run via treatment/source-water change and asserting mortality drops afterward while nitrite stays high.","Medium: the unit coverage still misses the explicit mortality comparison from the acceptance criteria. `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:1795-1837` only asserts higher `hourly_nitrite_stress_accum` under low chloride; it never checks that mortality is higher in the otherwise identical low-chloride/high-nitrite case.","Medium: the diagnosability requirement is only partially implemented. `crates/tank_core/src/systems/events.rs:29-48` reports NO2, chloride, ratio, and effective hazard, while `crates/tank_core/src/tracing.rs:270-344` reports raw nitrite/chloride pools and accumulated nitrite stress, but no output reports the stress contribution derived from the effective hazard, and effective hazard itself is not present in tracing/debug data."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Rewrite the integration scenario so one run enters a nitrite crisis first, then receives a chloride-raising treatment mid-run, ideally through the existing water-change/source-water path, and assert post-treatment mortality is lower even though nitrite remains elevated.","Add a unit-scale mortality test that exercises the existing mortality path for matched low- and high-chloride high-nitrite states and compares deaths or death probability, not just stress accumulation.","Expose the chloride-adjusted nitrite stress calculation in one diagnosable output surface by including NO2, chloride, effective hazard, and the resulting nitrite stress increment or accumulator together, then add a focused test for that output."],"outcome":"request_changes"}